Origin and attribution
----------------------

The pairing service is a continuation of the open-source project
rport-pairing (CloudRadar GmbH, 2022) and its community fork
openrport/rport-pairing (the openrport authors, 2023-2025). Both
upstreams shipped their source under the MIT License.

This repository imports the upstream Go source tree and rebrands it.
The upstream MIT-licensed portions remain covered by their original
MIT terms (see LICENSE-MIT for the inherited notice). The combined
work, as distributed by Proximile LLC under the name ProxiPort, is
AGPL-3.0-or-later.


Bundled third-party FOSS components
-----------------------------------

ProxiPort pairing uses the following FOSS Go modules without
modification. Each retains its own license. See the upstream project
for the authoritative copy.

- gorilla/mux — BSD-3-Clause (HTTP routing).
- patrickmn/go-cache — MIT (in-memory pairing-code cache).
- spf13/viper — MIT (TOML config loader).
- go-playground/validator — MIT (deposit-payload validation).
- iancoleman/strcase — MIT (validation-error formatting).
- matoous/go-nanoid — MIT (pairing-code generator).
- stretchr/testify — MIT (test assertions).

The transitive module graph is reproducible from go.mod / go.sum; all
modules listed there are FOSS-licensed.


